      {
        "id": 87021,
        "name": "Oaktree",
        "username": "Oaktree",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-20T06:12:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've been able to teach new people the game over the last month while still getting solo (and some forum play) in.&nbsp; So I get a mix of \"newbie games\" in while also still getting used to the heroes and such from the RC/IR expansions.&nbsp; Some interesting highlights in the past few days that show that the game can always be interesting in new ways:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Group with 3-4 games under their belt and having just trashed Akash'Bhuta got tossed The Dreamer as a curveball.&nbsp; Went down heavy in the 2nd half of the game as a swarm of projections proved too much along with the Dreamer herself inflicting damage.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>A 3-hero solo game I thought would be a boring kill (Nightmist, Young Legacy, AZ vs Baron Blade @ Insula Primalis) was anything but.&nbsp; Ended up with Nightmist in Mist Form fighting a flipped Blade and a swarm of dinosaurs.&nbsp; Game ended with a Volcanic Eruption finishing off Blade literally micro-seconds before it got Nightmist.&nbsp; (In other words, they both went down, but by rule I was able to make Baron Blade be snuffed first for the win.)</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>[Plus the realization that having an incap AZ giving Nightmist a +2 damage bonus to her next damage and having it accumulate for <em>five turns</em> is not necessarily a good thing for Nightmist when she has no chance to get a certain piece of equipment out first.]&nbsp;  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/blush.png?v=9\" title=\":blush:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":blush:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
